# Local Wrangler auth for the getmental.dev site.
#
# Copy this file to website/.env and fill the two blanks. .env is gitignored.
# Wrangler loads website/.env when you run commands from the website/ directory
# (https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/wrangler/system-environment-variables/).
#
# Production deploys still run in GitHub Actions (.github/workflows/deploy-website.yml).
# Put the same two values in the repo's Actions secrets. Do not commit either value.
#
# During `wrangler dev`, Wrangler also copies .env into the local Worker env object.
# The site code does not read these names. Do not log `env`.

# Account that owns the getmental Worker and the getmental.dev zone.
# Cloudflare dashboard → Workers & Pages. The id is the first path segment of the
# URL: https://dash.cloudflare.com/<account-id>/workers/overview
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/fundamentals/account/find-account-and-zone-ids/
# GitHub: Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=

# API token Wrangler uses instead of `wrangler login`.
# Cloudflare dashboard → My Profile → API Tokens → Create Token →
# use the "Edit Cloudflare Workers" template.
# https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens
# Scope the token to this one account and the getmental.dev zone.
# GitHub: the same secret name, CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN.
# Do not use the account Global API Key (CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY + CLOUDFLARE_EMAIL).
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=

# --- Not in this file ---
#
# NPM_TOKEN
#   GitHub Actions secret only, already set on afaraha8403/mental.
#   release.yml maps it to NODE_AUTH_TOKEN for `npm publish`.
#   Create or rotate at https://www.npmjs.com/settings/~/tokens
#   (Automation token, publish on the @balacode scope).
#   Do not copy it here. A laptop `npm publish` is not the release path.
#
# Decision-model keys (TypeSafe, OpenAI, Cloudflare Clef, custom)
#   Not environment variables. `mental option decide key <KEY>` writes
#   ~/.mental/config.json. MENTAL_JEV_KEY, TYPESAFE_API_KEY, and MENTAL_JEV_URL
#   are ignored.
#
# Optional shell flags for the CLI. They are not secrets and this file does
# not set them (the CLI does not load website/.env):
#   MENTAL_SKIP_UPDATE_CHECK=1     skip `npm view` for a newer CLI
#   MENTAL_NO_HINTS=1              silence the "decision model available" hint
#   MENTAL_ASCII=1                 strip emoji from TTY output
#   MENTAL_DIR=/path               force a bundle directory
#   SITE_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:4321
#                                  website/scripts/capture-site.mjs only
